<title>UK: Scottish Television H1 profits up 39 pct.</title>
<headline>Scottish Television H1 profits up 39 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30 1996</p>
<p>			    (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		11.5p		  vs 10.3p</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 5.5p		   vs 4.0p</p>
<p> Pretax		     10.3		   vs 7.4</p>
<p> Turnover		   52.2		   vs 46.9</p>
<p>NOTE - Scottish Television Plc said in a statement:</p>
<p>Following the strong performance in the first half of the year, we are confident of achieving satisfactory growth in the full year.&quot; It said the 38 pct rise in the interim dividend should not be interpreted as a measure of the rise in the final dividend.</p>
<p> Operating result	 8.8		    vs 7.0</p>
<p> Exceptional (cost)     0.5		    vs 0.3</p>
<p> Interest		   1.2		    vs 0.2</p>
<p> Tax payable		3.4		    vs 2.5</p>
<p> Attributable	     6.925		  vs 4.967</p>
<p> Pay date		   Nov 8</p>
<p>Div registration date  Oct 22 -- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
